# carts/dialogue - walkthrough, second answer: the same reading, the OTHER branch
# ("Row out with the lantern"), which finishes on the ending THE SHOAL LIGHT.
#
#     quarp replay record carts/dialogue -o /tmp/wa.qrpr --ticks 800 #         --input-file carts/dialogue/replays/walkthrough-alt.input
#
# Identical to walkthrough.input except for one thing: a Down tap is dropped in between
# every pair of X taps. Down does nothing at all while a line is being read, and the
# choice menu clamps at its last option instead of wrapping, so a Down tap is a no-op
# everywhere except the one place it matters and repeating it costs nothing. That is why
# this file, like its twin, does not have to know on which tick the menu shows up - and
# why the pair of them proves the branch and not the timing. It is also why re-wrapping the
# scene for 160x90 (ADR-021) could not desynchronise the pair: the menu moved 100 ticks
# earlier and the Down tap that selects the second option moved with it, unedited.
#
# Timeline on 160x90 (track-scale ticks; the cartridge sees entry N on its own tick N+1):
# the menu opens on tick 460, the Down tap on tick 470 moves the cursor to the second option
# (this is the first tick on which the two tracks draw different pixels), the tap on tick 480
# confirms it, and from tick 660 the screen is THE SHOAL LIGHT and frozen. Both branches
# happen to run to the same tick - they are five windows each.
10:D,11:,20:X,21:,30:D,31:,40:X,41:,
50:D,51:,60:X,61:,70:D,71:,80:X,81:,
90:D,91:,100:X,101:,110:D,111:,120:X,121:,
